spec:
  grid: 7-8 rows x 7-12 cols; background BLACK, single foreground color TEAL [observed]
  rectangles:
    count: 1-2 incomplete rectangles per grid
    height: always 4 rows
    width: 4 or 8 cols
    fill_ratio: 0.44-0.69 of bbox cells are foreground (rest are missing/bg)
    fragments: 1-4 disconnected 4-connected foreground fragments per rectangle group
    merging: fragments belong to same rectangle if their bboxes share any row or column span (transitive)
  separation:
    between_groups: bboxes of distinct rectangle groups must NOT share any row span or column span
    gap: at least 1 row AND 1 col of pure bg between group bboxes [observed]
  transform:
    for each merged group bbox, fill all bg cells inside with RED; foreground and bg outside unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid dims (7-8 rows, 7-12 cols) and num_groups (1-2).
    2. Place non-overlapping 4-tall rectangle bboxes (width 4 or 8) ensuring no shared row or column span between groups, with >=1 row/col gap.
    3. For each bbox, create a full solid rectangle (this is the output state: TEAL + RED fill).
    4. Randomly assign ~44-69% of bbox cells as TEAL foreground; remaining cells become bg (BLACK) in the input. Ensure the TEAL cells form at least 1 fragment whose 4-connected components, when merged by row/col bbox overlap, unify into the full bbox.
    5. Verify: running the solver's merge logic on the fragments recovers the original bbox for each group.
    6. Output = input with missing cells (bg inside each group bbox) recolored RED.
```
